      "side": 1,
      "message": "in the worst case it will be linear insertion time for each object path\n\nhttps://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_53_0/doc/html/boost/container/flat_set.html\n\nAnd why do we need boost container, there is an STL implementation.\n\nout of curiosity my coding agent microbenchmarked this and at least for the largest configuration i know `configurations/meta/ventura2/ventura2_canbus.json`, the `std::set` is twice as good in terms of runtime and saves around 100 us.\n\nSince there is no limit to the amount of configuration records, should we select a collection like `std::set` that does not have linear insertion overhead?\n\nFor the average configuration, this sacrifices only a few microseconds but it scales much better.",
